ws:\n\n- **`^(?=.*\\bIPV4\\b)`** — Ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address (using positive lookahead)\n- **`.*?\\b(DATEPATTERN)\\b`** — Matches everything up to and captures a YYYY-MM-DD date, with word boundaries to prevent partial matches like \"user1234-12-25\"\n- **`(?!.*\\bDATEPATTERN\\b)`** — Negative lookahead ensuring no more dates follow on the same line, guaranteeing only the last date is captured\n\nThe IPv4 octet pattern `(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9]?[0-9])` handles all values 0-255 without leading zeros. The date pattern allows months 01-12 and days 01-31 (including Feb 29), and word boundaries prevent false matches like \"1134-12-1234\" from being captured.","ttft_ms":107119,"type":"result","duration_ms":116469,"uuid":"4b62114b-bf69-4d8a-a43b-cb0f9b9d5f62","ttft_stream_ms":929,"time_to_request_ms":75,"queued_turn_count":0}
